<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Animism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as animist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Animism refers to religious beliefs that attribute spiritual presence to natural features, animals, places and ancestors. Such traditional religions were widely practised in West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, the royal court maintained traditional religion alongside Muslim traders, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> non-Muslim populations practising such beliefs were raided for captives.</p></div>
